  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	Pilot-Province &#x2018;Data and M&amp;E-Reporting&#x2019; systems and procedures are functional and design is more inclusive than at the start of the project and compared to other Provinces
-	Pilot-Province PCGG has a long-term Organisational strategy for becoming a state of the art resource/training centre, including training strategy and approach for strengthening inclusiveness of PLG decision &amp; policy making, GRID and LG basic service delivery
-	Number of published policy papers of each (i) Municipality Association of Nepal (MuAN), and (ii) Nepal Association of Rural Municipalities in Nepal (NARMIN) on LG decision-making and BSD, with specific focus on LG capacity for and responsiveness to inclusive ways of working, GESI objectives and GRID.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	TBD
-	PCGG Organisation Strategy includes no or limited GRID and GESI objectives and targeted CD activities
-	xx% of Women and Dalit-women ward members and LG staff (intended beneficiaries of PCGG services), which perceive PCGG strategy and services as adequately systemically inclusive
-	xx number of published policy papers over 2018-2021</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	Mid-term review (MTR) of the Provincial and Local Governance Support and Programme (PLGSP) conducted to inform government partners.
-  Third Party Monitoring (TPM) conducted to provide quality assurance for the smooth implementation of PLGSP
-  Retention strategy drafted and implemented
-  Conduct training on Gender and Social Inclusion (GESI) for the TA and Government officials
-  Conduct training to the capacity development officials of PLGSP and Government staffers on curricula development, needs assessment etc. 
-  Conduct Need Assessment of Provincial Center for Good Governance (PCGG)
-  Data and M&amp;E-Reporting&#x2019; systems and procedures produce required data and reports 50% more dis-aggregated data available for GESI and 50% more GESI indicators in LG progress reports
-  Conduct the Mapping of the Basic Service Delivery (BSD) in selected local bodies
-	PCGG Strategy includes an holistic approach and Plan to deliver GRID and GESI responsive CD services for strengthening PLG system inclusiveness and achieving PLG GESI objectives, including specific GESI trainings

-	Training outcome monitoring system in place for continuous learning and adaptation on GRID and GESI CD approach and interventions

-	100% increase in % of 1) PCGG and  2) PLG staff, which perceive PCGG strategy and services as inclusive - Assessment of PCGG existing strategy and training, PCGG and PLG staff perception survey on inclusiveness of PCGG strategy and services

-	Minimum #3 or 100% increase of publications by MuAN and Minimum #2 or 100% increase of publications by NARMIN
- Conduct GESi training for the officials of local bodies</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
